# Normalise to LF in the repo and in the working tree, on every platform.
# Without this, Git for Windows' default core.autocrlf=true checks source
# files out as CRLF -- oxfmt (`pnpm format:check`) rejects them, while
# `git status` still reports the tree clean, so the failure looks causeless.
# CI runs on ubuntu-24.04 and never sees the problem either.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets -- never touch these.
*.ico   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
